From 4808e030b598bf02e6102066f66738dd768db177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:48:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Suggest sets from the participant's side, one hair id per
 style, outfits per body
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three gaps found when the setup suggestions were reviewed on 10 Nov:

- Sets: the first suggested set could be the view from the staff side of a
  desk (airport test: "Check In Desk · Standing Behind Desk" for a check-in
  agent character). Each public set now carries the side its view is drawn
  from, read from its backdrop's reviewed interaction record (123 modern
  sets: 14 customer-side, 7 staff-side, 102 both). One-sided lines say so,
  the setup AI names participantSide (customer, service-provider or none),
  and the server drops and logs a suggested set drawn from the other side.
  participantSide is not sent on to the Studio.
- Hair: the generator was sent every race copy of every hair id (873
  women's and 665 men's ids for 106 and 116 styles and colours). It now gets
  one id per style and colour, and the hair id it returns is checked against
  that list like the outfit ids (logged and dropped when unknown). The
  whole request is 45% smaller on the local database copy.
- Outfits: an outfit id used on both bodies took its name and labels from
  whichever row came first, so the women's high_school_teacher and
  taxi_driver read the men's outfit. Each gender now reads only its own
  bodies' catalogue rows.

Checked with the real list code on the local database copy; not yet checked
with real AI answers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
